# oracle: fix rigid with fix_modify bodyforces late and a later fix addforce (adds forces after the rigid fix's post_force)
# oracle-compare: rel=1e-10 abs=1e-12 atomrel=1e-10
# Measured with native LAMMPS (probe runs, 64 atoms): the largest absolute thermo difference, pressure columns included, is 3.1e-13 (pzz); the per-atom scaled error is 1.0e-13. The rigid virial is exact only with the omega of the half-step quaternion that math_extra.cpp richardson() leaves in omega (the engine had the omega of the full-step quaternion, which put about 1e-8 into pxx and pyy).
units           lj
lattice         sc 0.5
region          box block 0 4 0 4 0 4
create_box      1 box
create_atoms    1 box
mass            1 1.0
variable        bid atom floor(x/2.0)+3*floor(y/2.5)
fix             1 all rigid custom v_bid
variable        vx atom 0.3*sin(0.9*x+0.4*z)
variable        vy atom 0.3*cos(0.6*y+0.8*x)
variable        vz atom 0.3*sin(0.7*z-0.3*y)
velocity        all set v_vx v_vy v_vz units box
pair_style      lj/cut 2.5
pair_coeff      1 1 1.0 1.0
timestep        0.002
fix             2 all addforce 0.05 -0.02 0.03
thermo_style    custom step temp pe ke etotal press pxx pyy pzz pxy pxz pyz f_1 f_1[1][1] f_1[1][4] f_1[4][7] f_1[4][10] f_1[2][13]
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
thermo          10
run             60
